   (u_s=2); compile p.209 rather than applying Prop. 6.3.
6. **Screened cofinality:** useful for targets, below coefficients in proof
   value; a finite negative scan is not eventual emptiness.

The lost CDC listing, edgewise recentering, and a stronger semigroup scalar
rank below these.  They can simplify a target list; none presently attacks
the existence of one pair.

### Disproof bottlenecks, in order

1. **One exact (D=108) full-tree coefficient point;** local stars, formal
   prefixes, and descendants are not enough.
2. **One inverse-descent edge;** Prop. 6.3 is one-way, so a descendant
