## 4. Idea cards (three maximum)

### Card 1 — the exact sibling scheme: barycentric nodes, edge fibre product

**Mechanism.**  At a full-tree node (v), write (P=P_v=\deg p_v),
(Q=Q_v=\deg q_v), let (a_1,\ldots,a_Q) be the distinct roots of the
squarefree (q_v), and let (u_i=\operatorname{mult}_{a_i}p_v), including
(u_i=0) at unused (q)-roots.  Define (w_i=P-Qu_i).  Prop. A.3 is

\[
Pp_vq_v'-Qq_vp_v'=c_vp_v,\qquad c_v\ne0.
\]

At (a_i), the reviewed local calculation gives

\[
w_iq_v'(a_i)=c_v.                                      \tag{4.1}
\]

The standard barycentric identities
(sum_i a_i^j/q_v'(a_i)=0) for (0\le j\le Q-2) therefore turn A.3 into
the weighted Vandermonde equations

\[
\sum_{i=1}^{Q}w_i a_i^j=0\quad(0\le j\le Q-2),\qquad
\sum_iw_i a_i^{Q-1}=c_v                              \tag{4.2}
\]

when (q_v) is monic.  Conversely, after saturating by
(Delta(q_v)c_v) and imposing (w_i\ne0), (4.2) makes the vector
((w_i)) proportional to ((1/q_v'(a_i))).  The polynomial

\[
E=Pq_v'-Qq_vp_v'/p_v
\]

then has degree at most (Q-1) and takes the same value (c_v) at all
(Q) roots of (q_v), so (E=c_v) and A.3 follows.  Thus this is an exact
node scheme, not an equation count or a passport analogy.  The local source
identity is checked in `xmodel/whole-tree-review-grok46-20260903.md:456-492`.

The uniform answer to `OPEN[SIBLING-COEFFICIENTS]` is **not** the product of
these node schemes.  It is their fibre product over the edge transition
maps, with the global polynomiality equations appended.  The dictionary is:

| Whole-tree object | Coefficient datum |
|---|---|
| node (v) | one actual local factor polynomial pair (p_v,q_v), its root-position scheme (4.2), degrees (P_v,Q_v), radius and centre |
| factor/child edge (v\to w) | a declared zero/nonzero factor label, multiplicity, coordinate substitution (\pi_v=C_{vw}(t)+t^{\delta_w-\delta_v}\pi_w), and the induced initial/jet map |
| sibling packet | all factors in the orbit partition, including unused (q)-roots; not merely the selected (V)-flag |
| leaf | a truncated root series (\tau_i), not automatically a physical place until the whole edge system is realized |
| Galois orbit | the actual permutation action, stabilizer character, shared coefficients, and one integration constant per complete branch orbit |
| ancestor | the shared outer units in (D_i=\prod_{j\ne i}(\tau_i-\tau_j)); descendants do not receive independent copies |
| root of the tree | the invariant sums giving `DEG`, `POLY`, and `NO-RESIDUE`; distinct orbit contributions may cancel only here |

This dictionary is forced by the exact tree factorizations and local/global
separation in `xmodel/global-interpolation-sol56-20260902.md:240-392` and
its minimal decorated input at lines 500-514.  It explicitly separates a
cv flag, a factor root, a branch series, and any eventual physical place.

**Dependencies.**  The Opus whole-tree review must pass; the screen must
export every orbit partition, not one representative witness; edge chart
maps and coefficient sharing must be supplied by the sibling lane; rings,
generator order, discriminants, and every saturation factor must be explicit.

**Bounded quantity and cheapest discriminator.**  Start with exactly the two
stored (D=108) variants at
`box/mohprog-drivers-20260903/tree-independent-passport-D48-120.json:1214`
and `:1263`.  Solve each node scheme separately, then form only the first
