### Card 3 — turn the (j=2) forced-zero pattern into a divisor theorem

**Mechanism.**  For an (s=3) row put

\[
X=n-M_2,\quad K=d_2,\quad r=d_3,\quad v=V_3.
\]

Here (M_3=n-2), (r\mid K,X),
(P=vK/r), (Q=vX/r), and Def. 5.1(3) gives

\[
\delta_2=1-{X(2v-r)\over vX-r}
={X(r-v)-r\over vX-r}.
\]

Let (B=vX-r) and
(G=\gcd(B,X(r-v)-r)=\gcd(B,r(X-2))).  The reduced denominator is
(A_2=B/G), while Euclid gives

\[
rB-vr(X-2)=r(2v-r),\qquad G\mid r(2v-r).              \tag{4.3}
\]

If (X>K), then the major threshold (h=K/X<1).  At (s=3) the
(j=2) parent is still `danger`.  A positive canonical zero residue
(b_0=P\bmod A_2) is at least one, hence exceeds (h), forces a major
zero sibling, and reaches Prop. 5.6.  Survival therefore requires
(A_2\mid P), and consequently

\[
vX-r\mid vK(2v-r).                                    \tag{4.4}
\]

For fixed ((K,r,v)), (X=(d+r)/v) comes from a divisor
(d\mid vK(2v-r)) with (d\equiv-r\pmod v).  This is an exact finite
parameterization, not a ceiling and not sufficiency.

For (s>3), fix the entire higher DP state and set

\[
C=\prod_{j=3}^{s}(V_j(n-M_j)-d_j),\quad
E=(n-M_s-1)\prod_{j=4}^{s}(V_j(n-M_{j-1})-d_j),
\]

with (L=L_2).  Then (L\delta_2=U(X)/W(X)), where

\[
U=L[(EV_3-C)X-Ed_3],\qquad W=E(V_3X-d_3),
\]

and the content-correct statement is

\[
\gcd(U(X),W(X))\mid |LEd_3C|.                         \tag{4.5}
\]

On a still-dangerous (j=2) state with (X>K), the same reasoning makes
(W(X)) divide a fixed statewise carrier after primitive reduction.  A
nonzero ancestor can clear `danger`, so (4.5) must be a DP-state rule, never
a scalar row filter.

**Dependencies.**  The promoted `danger` semantics and full higher
(V)-tuple; exact reduced denominators; no edgewise recenter conjecture.

**Bounded quantity and cheapest discriminator.**  Verify (4.4) on every
(s=3) member among the 2,824 `C_FULL_TREE_ODE` assignments through
(D\le200), then emit the primitive carrier divided by (N) on every
still-dangerous (j=2) state through (D\le400).  This is integer
arithmetic in the running screen, expected seconds and under 1 GB.

**Outcomes.**

- Carrier/(N) is uniformly bounded and divisor choices stabilize: promote
  a precise all-degree lemma target coupling the pin to (4.5).
- It grows on a screened parametric family: stop the skeleton-ceiling route
  and bank that family as the coefficient/counterexample target list.
- The equivalence fails on a control: repair denominator/content or danger
  propagation; no mathematical inference.

**Stop condition.**  One growing exact family, or any need to discard the
full DP state, stops the ceiling claim.  No extrapolation from (D\le400).

**Expected information gain.**  High at negligible cost.  It either exposes
the arithmetic theorem behind the repeated (b_{\min}>h) kills or turns
