## 8. What generalizes

There is **no** h_pi-absorption lemma depending only on `u_s=1` and `k>=2`.
Equation (5.4) shows that absorption depends on the actual correction module,
and the primitive smooth component shows that the monomial exponent alone is
not an obstruction. The first proof-shaped uniform statement is instead:

> For each licensed inherited state and each first Newton weight/Kummer
> character in which the bottom residual occurs, the class of
> `gamma^k h_pi` is outside the image of the associated-graded linearized
> correction map; nonlinear terms are triangular in later weights.

That statement would imply failure by induction on weight, but it requires
the whole inherited support and a proof of triangularity. It is not presently
proved for every `u_s=1` descendant.

