Therefore the top two blocks accept the very slice whose ramification they
were meant to reject. Whether legal `alpha,R,beta` corrections cancel the
nonconstant part is a **bottom-block image question**, and remains open until
the height-three support is licensed. An empty saturation of any guessed
two-page Newton slice would be `SLICE-EMPTY`, not a target kill.

### 5.3 Kummer characters

After adjoining `mu_4` if necessary (otherwise read this as the finite-free
`Z/4` grading), put `X=gamma^4/4` and decompose

\[
P=\sum_{a=0}^3\gamma^aP_a(X,\pi),\qquad
Q=\sum_{b=0}^3\gamma^bQ_b(X,\pi).
\]

This declares the ring map

\[
K[X,\pi]\hookrightarrow K[\gamma,\pi],\qquad X\mapsto\gamma^4/4;
\]

it does not identify the variable names. With
`E_a=a+4X partial_X`, multiplication of the Jacobian equation by `gamma`
gives character block `ell`:

\[
\sum_{a+b\equiv\ell\ (4)}
(4X)^{\lfloor(a+b)/4\rfloor}
\big(E_aP_a\,Q_{b,\pi}-P_{a,\pi}E_bQ_b\big)
=\begin{cases}4cX,&\ell=0,\\0,&\ell=1,2,3.\end{cases} \tag{5.5}
\]

The dense coefficient buckets are

```text
P: (54,50,45,40)     Q: (27,24,21,18)
raw [P,Q] residues: (120,112,105,98)
